<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθεῖος</span></b> , also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trusty,
				honoured</i>, term of address used to express respect, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθεῖε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.518
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				103
			</span></i>: periphr., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθείη κεφαλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.94
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλά μιν ἠθεῖον καλέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.147
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεῖνον ἐμὸν ἠθαῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					2.48
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθαῖοι</span>
			<i>trusty friends</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
				22
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦθος</span>.)</div>
